As for referring to poly/rust traps as magic traps: whoops.

Rust traps are quite possibly the most annoying trap type ever. Sure,
polymorph traps can destroy your armor, but there are amulets of
unchanging and rings of polymorph for that. Also the chances of turning
into a monster that breaks your armor are rather low. There is only one
way to protect oneself from a rust trap, however, and cans of grease
are extremely rare, in my opinion (the damage can also be repaired with
oil, which is slightly less rare, but only provides a single usage).
The way I see it, the best way to not get your weapons/armor ruined by
traps is to have the searching intrinsic.

While we're on the topic, I guess we can also talk about equipment
(weapons and armor) being ruined by other means. As far as I know,
there are two few other ways by which the game will try to ruin your
armor or weapon: fire traps and monsters.

Fire traps can be detected, or even protected against with fire
resistance. Or better yet, not wearing cloth, leather, or wood not
disables the fire trap from ruining your armor (items like scrolls are
still vulnerable though).

The following monsters have acidid splashing attacks that can corrode
equipment: acid blob, ochre jelly, spotted jelly, green mold. The
yellow dragon has an acidic breath attack that can corrode equipment.
The black naga has an acidic spitting attack, but this cannot corrode.
Juiblex has an acidic spitting attack, which I assume cannot corrode,
since the black naga's acidic spit cannot corrode, though I haven't
actually tested it yet. Additionally, the rust monster can rust
equipment, the gray ooze can rust armor only, and the black pudding can
corrode equipment. Rust and corrosion CAN stack! (only applies to iron
equipment) The states are independent of each other, though the
detriments are cumulative.

The following monsters have fire breath attacks that can burn armor
(not weapons) and things like scrolls: hell hound pup, hell hound, red
dragon, red naga, Ixoth. The fire ant, salamander, fire elemental, and
pyrolisk have fire attacks that can destroy things like scrolls, but
not equipment. The flaming sphere, steam vortex, red mold, and fire
vortex have fire attacks that cannot destroy anything.

Brown puddings are the only monsters with a rotting attack that I know
of. This attack can rot armor only. Not weapons, and not inventory
items.

I made sure to use objects made of the appropriate materials when I did
all my tests (e.g. wielded organic weapons, wore organic armor, and had
organic inventory items when being attacked by brown pudding).

An interesting thing is that although weapons are subject to rust and
corrosion, I was unable to make them burn or rot. Monster attacks
didn't burn/rot wooden wielded weapons (even when I attacked the
monsters with the weapons), and fire traps didn't burn wielded wooden
weapons. What's the deal with that?



